---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Tag from '../components/Tag.astro';
import TechList from '../components/TechList.astro';
import Bullets from '../components/Bullets.astro';
import { links } from '../data/site';
import { lagos } from '../data/lagos';
import heroMap from '../assets/images/lagos-hero-map.png';
import pipeline from '../assets/images/lagos-pipeline.svg';
import beforeAfter from '../assets/images/lagos-before-after.png';
import candidate from '../assets/images/lagos-candidate-detail.png';
import coverage from '../assets/images/lagos-coverage-map.png';

const wide = '(min-width: 1024px) 960px, 100vw';
const h2 = 'text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900';
---

<Base
  title="Lagos Flood Intelligence | Waheed Odubayo"
  description="A reproducible Sentinel-1 radar change pipeline for mapping candidate flooded areas in Lagos after the July 2024 floods."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <a href="/#products" class="text-sm font-medium text-ocean-600 hover:text-ocean-700">← All products</a>

    <header class="mt-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <Tag>Geospatial pipeline</Tag>
        <Tag tone="progress">In progress</Tag>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">{lagos.title}</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg text-slate-600">{lagos.intro}</p>
      <a href={links.lagosRepo} class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium text-ocean-600 hover:text-ocean-700">
        View on GitHub →
      </a>
    </header>

    <figure class="mt-10">
      <Image src={heroMap} alt="Map of the Lagos coast with small candidate patches along the coastline and lagoons" widths={[640, 960, 1600]} sizes={wide} class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200" />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">{lagos.mapCaption}</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <h2 class={h2}>The pipeline</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-slate-700">
        Five stages, each producing auditable outputs: acquire a before/after Sentinel-1 pair,
        preprocess it in ESA SNAP, compare backscatter in decibels, extract candidate patches, and
        validate them against independent evidence.
      </p>
      <figure class="mt-6">
        <Image src={pipeline} alt="Workflow: acquire, preprocess, compare, candidates, validate (incomplete)" class="w-full rounded-lg" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <h2 class={h2}>Before, after, and the change</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-slate-700">
        Radar sees through cloud — essential in a rainy-season flood. Open water reflects the radar
        signal away from the satellite, so newly flooded ground tends to appear darker. Comparing
        the same window before and after the event highlights where that darkening happened.
      </p>
      <figure class="mt-6">
        <Image src={beforeAfter} alt="Three radar panels of the same area: 21 June 2024, 3 July 2024, and the change between them" widths={[640, 960, 1600]} sizes={wide} class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          Radar backscatter on 21 June and 3 July 2024, and the change between them.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-5">
      <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        <h2 class={h2}>Why “candidates,” not “floods”</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">{lagos.whyCandidates}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">
          Candidate C0079, on the edge of Ologe Lagoon, shows why: a strong radar drop, flat
          terrain — but it overlaps historical water, so its flood status stays unknown until
          independent evidence settles it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="lg:col-span-3">
        <Image src={candidate} alt="Close-up of candidate C0079 on the eastern margin of Ologe Lagoon with its review attributes" widths={[640, 960, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 580px, 100vw" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <h2 class={h2}>Knowing what we can’t see</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-slate-700">
        71% of the study area had usable radar measurements on both dates. The rest — mostly lagoon
        water and a strip outside the radar footprint — is excluded, not assumed dry.
      </p>
      <figure class="mt-6">
        <Image src={coverage} alt="Map of the Lagos study area showing 71.05% of pixels with usable measurements on both dates" widths={[640, 960, 1600]} sizes={wide} class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          Coverage is a valid-data fraction, not a flood-accuracy score.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 grid gap-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 sm:p-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Progress so far</h2>
        <Bullets items={lagos.progress} />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Next</h2>
        <Bullets items={lagos.next} />
        <TechList items={lagos.tech} />
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
